          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            There exist various
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            structures which
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} present
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} L-∞ algebras
          %p
            By definition
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} L-∞ algebras
            are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-algebras"} ∞-algebras
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+chain+complexes"} category of chain complexes
            over the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+operad"} Lie operad
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+algebras+over+an+operad"} model structure on algebras over an operad
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dg-Lie+algebras"} model structure on dg-Lie algebras
          %p
            A more geometric way is to think of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} L-∞ algebras
            as being the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+spaces"} tangent spaces
            to connected
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} smooth ∞-groupoids
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+%E2%88%9E-stacks"} moduli ∞-stacks
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groups"} smooth ∞-groups
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo ↪
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{B}\mathfrak{g} \hookrightarrow \mathbf{B}G
          %p
            of the essentially unique point
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} * \to \mathbf{B}G
            (see at
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+differentiation"} Lie differentiation
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+geometry"} formal
            neighbourhood (the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jets"} jets
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} associative algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coalgebra"} coalgebra
            (see at
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+algebra"} smooth algebra
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
          %p
            In particular, one succinct way to present
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} L-∞ algebras
            (as discussed there) is as
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-coalgebras"} dg-coalgebras
          #LInfinityAlgebraIsQuasiFreeDgCoalgebra.num_prop
            %h6#propositiondefinition Proposition/Definition
            %p
              An
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} L-∞ algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathfrak{g}, [-], [-,-], [-,-,-], \cdots)
              structure on a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+space"} graded vector space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              is equivalently a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-coalgebra"} dg-coalgebra
              structure on the graded-commutative
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofree+coalgebra"} cofree coalgebra
              over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔤
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            %p
              Conversely, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} L-∞ algebras
              (and general “weak” morphisms between them) is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              of that of counital cocommutative
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-coalgebras"} dg-coalgebras
              on those whose underlying bare graded-commutative
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coalgebra"} coalgebra
              (forgetting the codifferential) is free
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                    %mi Alg
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi dgCoCAlg
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    L_\infty Alg \hookrightarrow dgCoCAlg
                    \\,.
          %p
            Accordingly it is of interest to have also
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dg-coalgebras"} model structure on dg-coalgebras
            or dually (on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pro-objects"} pro-objects
            of)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebras"} dg-algebras
            which presents
            = succeed "-algebras." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LInfinityAlgebraIsFibrantObjectIndgFormalSpace"}
            below identifies the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mn ∞
                  %mi Alg
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty Alg
            as the (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"}> full sub-
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fibrant+objects"} category of fibrant objects
            inside such a model structure of “differential graded formal spaces”, which in turn is related by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zig-zag"} zig-zag
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
            to various other models
          .num_remark
            %h6#remarkwarning Remark/Warning
            %p
              So we write “
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                    %mi Alg
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty Alg
              ” here for the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-category"} 1-category
              of
              = succeed "-algebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
              of
              = succeed "-algebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
              = succeed "\u201D," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                      %mi Alg
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_W( L_\infty Alg)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+localization"} simplicial localization
              of this 1-category.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remarkwarning_2 Remark/Warning
            %p
              All gradings in the following are
              = succeed "-gradings," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
              this means that we are dealing with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+geometry"} derived geometry
              (see below the section
              %em
                %a{:href => "##SheavesOverCosimplicialInfinitesimallyThickenedPoints"} Simplicial sheaves over comsimplicial formal spaces
              for details): the algebra elements in positive degree correspond to
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} categorical
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} simplicial
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
              = succeed "-degree," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stack"} ∞-stack
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosimplicial+object"} cosimplicial
              degree of the derived site of cosimplicial formal spaces.
            %p
              Technically this affects for instance the nature of
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrations"} fibrations
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dg-Lie+algebras"} model structure on dg-Lie algebras
              %a{:href => "#OndgLieAlgebras"} below
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transferred+model+structure"} transferred
              from a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+chain+complexes"} model structure on chain complexes
              = succeed "\u201D" do
                %a{:href => "model+structure+on+chain+complexes#CategoricalProjectiveClass"} Categorical projective class structure
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+maps"} chain maps
              that are surjective in every degree. This appears for instance in prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ModelStructureOnDgLieAlgebras"}
              and prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LInfinityAlgebrasAsACategoryOfFibrantObjects"}
              below.
            %p
              On the other hand, if one considered chain complexes in non-negative degree (for tangent complexes in “higher but non-derived geometry”), then one would use the
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "model+structure+on+chain+complexes#ProjectiveStructureOnChainComplexes"} Projective structure on chain complexes in non-negative degree
              %em positive
              degree. This case is (currently)
              %em not
              discussed in the following.
          #NonWeakMaps.num_remark
            %h6#remarkwarning_3 Remark/Warning
            %p
              Some of the model structures below are on the category of
              = succeed "-algebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebras+over+an+operad"} algebras over an operad
              for an
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+resolution"} cofibrant resolution
              of the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+operad"} Lie operad
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi str
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                    %mi Alg
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    L_\infty Alg_{str} \to L_\infty Alg
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wide+subcategory"} wide subcategory
              on the strict
              = succeed "-morphisms." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
          %h2#definition_as_algebras_over_an_operad Definition as algebras over an operad
          %p
            As their name indicates,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} L-∞ algebras
            are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+algebras"} homotopy algebras
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+an+operad"} over
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+operad"} Lie operad
            (in a
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+chain+complexes"} category of chain complexes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structures+on+algebras+over+an+operad"} model structures on algebras over an operad
            provides a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            structure on the category of
            = succeed "-algebras." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
          %p
            This we discuss here. But there is also a natural identification of
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+object"} infinitesimal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+stack"} derived
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stacks"} ∞-stacks
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "#DefinitionsAndQuillenEquivalences"} Definitions as formal/infinitesimal ∞-stacks
          %p
            By the general discussion at
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dg-algebras+over+an+operad"} model structure on dg-algebras over an operad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            which contains the field of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rational numbers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+operad"} symmetric operad
            (uncolored)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒪
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+chain+complexes"} category of chain complexes
            (unbounded)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Ch
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ch_\bullet(k)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free-forgetful+adjunction"} free-forgetful adjunction
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Alg
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo →
                      %mi U
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi F
                  %msub
                    %mi Ch
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Alg(\mathcal{O})
                  \\stackrel{\overset{F}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{U}{\to}}
                  Ch_\bullet(k)
          %p
            between the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebras+over+an+operad"} algebras over an operad
            and the underlying chain complexes induces a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transferred+model+structure"} transferred model structure
            from the projective unbounded
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+chain+complexes"} model structure on chain complexes
            where hence on both sides
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the weak equivalences are the morphisms that are
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphisms"} quasi-isomorphisms
                on the (underlying) chain complexes;
            %li
              %p
                the fibrations are the morphisms that are degreewise
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjections"} surjections
                on the (underlying) chain complexes.
          %p
            Hence in particular
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (F \vdash U)
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
            between these model structures.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Hinich97"}> Hinich97, theorem 4.1.1
            )
          %p
            So this is in particular true for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo =
                  %mover
                    %mi Lie
                    %mo ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O} = \widehat Lie
            the standard
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+resolution"} cofibrant resolution
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+operad"} Lie operad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Alg
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mover
                    %mi Lie
                    %mo ^
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mn ∞
                  %msub
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi str
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg(\widehat Lie) \simeq L_\infty Alg_{str}
            is the category of (unbounded)
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            = succeed "-maps" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#NonWeakMaps"}
            above) and hence is equipped with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transferred+model+structure"} transferred model structure
            this way
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mn ∞
                  %msub
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi str
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo →
                      %mi U
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi F
                  %msub
                    %mi Ch
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  L_\infty Alg_{str}(k)
                  \\stackrel{\overset{F}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{U}{\to}}
                  Ch_\bullet(k)
                  \\,.
          %p
            Moreover, by the rectification result discussed at
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dg-algebras+over+an+operad"} model structure on dg-algebras over an operad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi Lie
                    %mo ^
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %mi Lie
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat Lie \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} Lie
            induces a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mn ∞
                  %msub
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi str
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %mi dgLieAlg
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  L_\infty Alg_{str}(k) \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} dgLieAlg(k)
          %p
            with the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dg-Lie+algebras"} model structure on dg-Lie algebras
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transferred+model+structure"} transferred
            from the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+chain+complexes"} model structure on chain complexes
          %h2#DefinitionsAndQuillenEquivalences
            Definitions as formal/infinitesimal
            = succeed "-stacks" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            We list here definitions of various further
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            structures that all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} present
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} L-∞ algebras
            and describe a web of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zig-zags"} zig-zags
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalences"} Quillen equivalences
            between them. These Quillen equivalences may be thought of as presenting an equivalence between the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            of
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+object"} infinitesimal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+stack"} derived
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stacks"} ∞-stacks
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+moduli+problems"}> formal moduli problems
            ”).
