          %p
            We discuss some further properties of the
            %a{:href => "DefinitionsAndQuillenEquivalences"} above
            model category structures.
          #RightProperness.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_16 Proposition
            %p
              The model category
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi dgFormalSpace
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dgFormalSpace
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#dgFormalSpace"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+proper+model+category"} right proper model category
          %p
            This observation has been communicated privately by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Pridham"} Jonathan Pridham
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              We need to show that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              of a weak equivalence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi w
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
              along a fibration
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is again a weak equivalence. If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi w
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
              is a fibration, this is automatic, so by factorisation we reduce to the case where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi w
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
              is a cofibration. Now, every trivial cofibration is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spf
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spf
              of a composition of acyclic small extensions, so we may take
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi w
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
              to be
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spf
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spf
              of an acyclic small extension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spf
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spf
              of a quasi-free map
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spf
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spf
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo →
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi IR
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \to R/IR
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi IR
                      %mo =
                      %mi I
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mi A
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} IR =I\hat{\otimes}_A R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi IR
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \to R/IR
              is also an acyclic small extension.
          %h3#HomotopiesAndDerivedHomSpaces Homotopies and derived hom spaces
          %p
            In any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            we have a notion of
